With “background-clip: text” and no text, Ladybird paints none of the
background that’s clipped to the text, which the other engines get from
an empty text mask: Blink’s BoxPainterBase::PaintFillLayerTextFillBox()
draws the background and masks it with a kDstIn layer that it fills
with the text, in PaintTextClipMask(). WebKit’s BackgroundPainter paints
the text into a mask for FillBox::Text, in paintMaskForTextFillBox(),
and clips the background to it. And Gecko’s GenerateAndPushTextMask()
shades the element’s text frames into an A8 mask, then blends the
background through that mask.
